cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset or pipeline, please cite it as below."
title: "slashyear: the year-by-year historical record, sourced line by line"
abstract: >-
  A corpus of dated historical events extracted from English Wikipedia year articles, in which
  every entry is quoted verbatim from a specific numbered revision and carries that revision id,
  article title and section anchor, so each row is mechanically checkable against its source.
  Includes the extraction pipeline, the published site, and the verification gates that prove
  every published sentence appears in the revision it cites.
type: dataset
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
url: "https://slashyear.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ctrl-maud/slashyear"
keywords:
  - history
  - chronology
  - timeline
  - wikipedia
  - open data
  - provenance
  - retrieval augmented generation
authors:
  - name: "slashyear"
    website: "https://slashyear.com"
